# #191 Lich into Shadow Hunter: a second powershield hands the missile back to the Lich
# a (Lich) fires its neutral special at 600 from x -240; b (Shadow Hunter) at x 240 powershields it with
# one full trigger press. A reflection sends back a's own projectile: same family (a's fighter
# code), kind and model, half damage, turned around and owned by b (the `reflect` line on b's
# trace), and it strikes a, never b. Frames come from replaying this script's inputs through the
# match step from the quick-pair start; not yet run headless here (no /dev/uinput).
# Syntax and checks: smashcraft:docs/native-bot-session.md.
#! chat -dev quick pair lich / shadow hunter
600 a tap X 2
644 b shield 1
674 b shield 0
# a powershields the returning projectile: it is a's again, still a's family, model and kind, at a quarter damage.
680 a shield 1
710 a shield 0
# View held a second: a moment the parity check replays.
740 a press VIEW
810 a release VIEW
#! expect b 645 reflect family 6 kind 5 model Abilities\Weapons\LichMissile\LichMissile.mdx direction -1 multiplier 0.500 life 51
#! expect a 681 reflect family 6 kind 5 model Abilities\Weapons\LichMissile\LichMissile.mdx direction 1 multiplier 0.250 life 15
#! absent a 600-681 damage
#! absent b 600-681 damage
